## What
Converts the catch-block `console.error` calls in 5 tenant API routes to structured `logError` from `@/lib/errors-server`:
`activities`, `audit`, `search`, `roles`, `segments` — **8 call sites**.

Each error now goes through the single funnel: persisted to `error_logs`, forwarded to Sentry + Loki (when enabled), and **request-id correlated** — `logError` reads the request id automatically from AsyncLocalStorage (`getCurrentRequestId`), so no `ctx` plumbing is needed at the call site.

```ts
// before
} catch (err) { console.error('[roles GET]', err); return apiError(err); }
// after
} catch (err) { await logError({ error: err, context: 'roles GET', requestMethod: 'GET' }); return apiError(err); }
```

## Deliberate decisions
- **No `tenantId`/`userId` added here.** `ctx` is declared inside the `try`, so it isn't in `catch` scope. Hoisting it is a larger, riskier change I'm keeping out of a mechanical batch. Request-id correlation already lands via ALS.
- **Scope:** ~404 `console.error` remain (app/api 90, lib 148, scripts 129, components 36). `lib`/`scripts`/`components` are intentionally deferred — many run outside a request/DB context where `logError`'s DB write is inappropriate (it would need different handling). Follow-up batches will cover the rest of `app/api/tenant` then `app/api`.

## Checks
