The `macos` GitHub Actions job was failing smoke checks tied to canvas/window size synchronization and stroke geometry stability on pen-up. This PR narrows the fix to the two runtime paths responsible for those failures.

- **Surface resize uses rendered box dimensions**
  - Updated `Surface.resize()` to derive logical canvas size from `getBoundingClientRect()` (rounded), instead of `clientWidth/clientHeight`.
  - This aligns surface width/height with actual stage-rendered dimensions across macOS resize/maximize/DPR transitions.

- **Stroke commit preserves drawn geometry**
  - Updated `finishStroke()` to keep captured stroke point precision when persisting ink, rather than rounding each point on pen-up.
  - Prevents visible shape drift between in-progress (wet) stroke rendering and committed stroke rendering.

```js
// surface.js
const box = this.canvas.getBoundingClientRect();
const w = Math.round(box.width), h = Math.round(box.height);

// tools.js
obj.points = obj.points.map((p) => ({ x: p.x, y: p.y, p: p.p ?? 0.5 }));
```

