## Objective
Replace the failed direct Safari -> EODHD path with a narrow server-side secret boundary while keeping all portfolio data local.

## Worker contract
- `GET /health`
- `GET /prices?benchmark=msci-world&from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`
- `GET /prices?benchmark=sp500&from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD`

## Security/privacy
- only two fixed public benchmark IDs are accepted;
- no arbitrary symbols and no portfolio payload endpoint exists;
- EODHD token is read only from Cloudflare secret `EODHD_API_TOKEN`;
- CORS is restricted to `https://alanb3110.github.io`;
- date ranges are limited to 370 days;
- provider payloads are sanitized to date + adjusted close;
- successful responses are cached for 6 hours to protect the free EODHD quota.

## Validation
CI now runs a Worker syntax check and smoke test covering CORS, allow-listing, date limits, sanitization and secret non-disclosure.

The PWA is not switched to the Worker URL in this PR because the final `workers.dev` URL is only known after the one-time Cloudflare deployment. The direct browser EODHD diagnostic remains temporary until that deployment is validated.

